CORE
main.c
--32 --unwind 2 --rounds 3 --allow-pointer-unsoundness --array-rf-bytes
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
--array-rf-bytes answers reads of an array that is accessed byte-wise (here a
heap array of non-constant size, written through a char or short pointer) byte
by byte from the writes covering each byte: no spurious violation.
